  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-116947",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Two angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, the measure of an angle that's supplementary to an angle of $(2x+65)^{∘}$ must be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}-(2x+65)^{∘} & =(180-2x-65)^{∘} \\\\  & =(180-65-2x)^{∘} \\\\  & =(115-2x)^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
